  "body": "Bf16PrefillKernel's consumers read a stage with ldmatrix (generic proxy) and release it; the producer then refills it with TMA (async proxy) without a proxy fence, so a refill can overwrite operands still being read. Add fence.proxy.async after producer_acquire, as the dense GEMM mainloop does (#16).\n\nFound by the b12x race tests (CUDA-graph replay under SM contention):\n- before: 1536x5120->1024 corrupted in 345 of 2000 replays on GB10 (77 of 2000 on an RTX PRO 6000), nearly the whole output off by about 20%; 2048x5120->384 208 of 2000.\n- after: the race tests' 5 BF16 projection cases (prefill, mma, tc, simt backends) pass on GB10; 0 of 3000 on the RTX PRO 6000.",
